cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the repository. An associated manuscript is in preparation."
title: "rbcL / Evo 2 — generative biology on a taxonomically structured gene family"
authors:
  - family-names: Oppong
    given-names: Yaa
    alias: YaaOppong
abstract: >-
  Prompt-conditioned generation and LoRA finetuning of
  the Evo 2 genomic foundation model on rbcL, the plastid gene encoding the
  Rubisco large subunit. Includes a shared evaluation harness and an analysis
  of clade-structured coverage gaps in the model's plastid training data.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YaaOppong/rbcl-generative-biology"
keywords:
  - genomic language models
  - Evo 2
  - LoRA
  - rbcL
  - Rubisco
  - sequence generation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Genome modelling and design across all domains of life with Evo 2"
    authors:
      - family-names: Brixi
        given-names: Garyk
      - family-names: Durrant
        given-names: Matthew G.
      - family-names: Ku
        given-names: Jerome
      - family-names: Hsu
        given-names: Patrick D.
      - family-names: Hie
        given-names: Brian L.
    journal: Nature
    volume: 652
    issue: 8112
    start: 1349
    end: 1361
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-026-10176-5
    notes: >-
      The model used throughout. 62 authors; first five listed. Preprint:
      bioRxiv 10.1101/2025.02.18.638918 (2025). Trained on 9.3T nucleotides;
      OpenGenome2 is the training corpus whose plastid partition Part A audits.
  - type: article
    title: "Sequence modeling and design from molecular to genome scale with Evo"
    authors:
      - family-names: Nguyen
        given-names: Eric
    journal: Science
    year: 2024
    notes: "Evo 1 — the predecessor model, cited for architectural lineage only."
  - type: article
    title: "Mining rbcL genes reveals novel Rubisco kinetics"
    authors:
      - family-names: Iqbal
        given-names: Wasim Ahmad
      - family-names: Lisitsa
        given-names: Andrei
      - family-names: Kapralov
        given-names: Maxim V.
    journal: "Journal of Experimental Botany"
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.1093/jxb/erac368
    notes: "Kinetics oracle reimplemented from this work (reported as a negative result)"
